title: IntroductionPart0
---
<<empty characterSprite>>
chip: this world is fucking miserable.
chip: you get up at the asscrack of dawn and work your tail off until the sun sets, and for what?
chip: you'll only ever be one measly little fish in a sea of people. or a number on some rich bastard's spreadsheet.

chip: nobody cares about who you are, or how you're doing, no, none of that. it's just about what you can do for them.
chip: and even if you do everything right, you STILL get fucked! 

narrator: chip kicks a rock while trudging down the sidewalk.

chip: ...
chip: god.
chip: this shit blows. 
chip: and not in the good way.

chip: depressed, single, AND laid off... yeah, what more could a guy want?

narrator: he sighs as he pulls a sleek black smartphone out of his back pocket and enters his passcode.

<<playerPhone characterSprite>>
chip: but whatever. he said he was at 38 hemingway street... "my address... see you at 2". with a purple heart at the end. ha.

<<empty characterSprite>>
chip: hopefully this'll get my mind off of all that garbage from earlier.
chip: alright, that's 86 hemingway. 
chip: ... and that's 90. 
chip: ...
chip: ... ... ...
chip: shit, i'm totally going in the wrong direction.

===
title: IntroductionPart1
---
<<chipNeutral characterSprite>>
chip: 34... 36... 
chip: there we go, 38. finally. and he said the apartment number was...

<<empty characterSprite>>
narrator: he checks his phone again.

<<chipNeutral characterSprite>>
chip: 20. cool.

<<empty characterSprite>>
narrator: chip pushes the "20" button on the panel next to the door and within seconds, hears a buzz.

<<chipNeutral characterSprite>>
chip: damn, okay, that was fast. someone's desperate...

<<empty characterSprite>>
narrator: the front door of the apartment building unlocks with a nice, crisp click. chip pushes it open.

<<chipNeutral characterSprite>>
chip: oh thank god, it's warm in here.

<<empty characterSprite>>
narrator: looking around, he doesn't see anything particularly eyecatching. couple of taiga packages lying on the ground, dust piling up in the corners...
narrator: it's almost like looking at a palette-swapped copy of his own apartment building. except...

<<chipNeutral characterSprite>>
chip: what floor was he on again? i'm only seeing 1-5 on the doors down here, so logically speaking... it'd at least be the fifth floor.
chip: now the real question is, does this place have an elevator?

<<empty characterSprite>>
narrator: upon further investigation, chip discovers that there is not, in fact, an elevator. tough luck.

<< chipNeutral characterSprite>>
chip: fuck. fine, this better be worth it.

<<empty characterSprite>>
narrator: he begrudgingly ascends five flights of stairs and winds up face to face with a quaint wooden door marked "20". it's cracked open just a hair.
narrator: out of respect, chip decides to knock anyway.

<<chipNeutral characterSprite>>
chip: hey, luce? or, luke? not sure how you'd say–

<<empty characterSprite>>
narrator: the door swings open, cutting him off mid-sentence.

<<luciGreeting characterSprite>>
lucifer: oh! hey! wow, i didn't think you'd get here so quickly. um, hi! haha! 

<<chipNeutral characterSprite>>
chip: hey–

<<luciGreeting characterSprite>>
lucifer: and i gueeeeess "luce" would be closer, but like, you can just call me luci. or lucifer. or whatever you want.

<<chipNeutral characterSprite>>
chip: sick. so... can i come in?

<<luciGreeting characterSprite>>
lucifer: oh yeah! make yourself at home. but, uh... i didn't really get the chance to clean up before you got here.
lucifer: hope that's alright. it's not thaaaat bad, just messy, haha! you know how it is sometimes. with work and stuff.

<<chipNeutral characterSprite>>
chip: mm, yeah, i hear you.


===
title: IntroductionPart2
---
<<chipNeutral characterSprite>>
chip: so, luce, when we talked earlier you said that you wanted me to–

<<luciNeutral characterSprite>>
lucifer: help me organize this place!

<<chipNeutral characterSprite>>
chip: pause. what?

<<luciNeutral characterSprite>>
lucifer: yeah... it's just been so hard lately, like–

<<chipNeutral characterSprite>>
chip: no, no, i understand that. but we NEVER talked about cleaning.

<<luciNeutral characterSprite>>
lucifer: oh. hm. must've been someone else then.
lucifer: by the way, uh, feel free to take that sweater off. my heater's busted, it's been hot as hell for forever and my landlord's, like, not responding.

<<chipNeutral characterSprite>>
chip: ... right. yeah, no ulterior motives behind your request, i'm sure.

<<chipShirtless characterSprite>>
chip: sorry about the heater, though.

<<luciBack characterSprite>>
lucifer: hehe, yeah. weeeeeeell, since you're here and you look like a big, strong, capable man, why don't you... help me out anyway?

<<chipShirtless characterSprite>>
chip: hmm... depends. what's in it for me?

<<luciPoint characterSprite>>
narrator: lucifer points at himself and smiles, garnering a chuckle from chip.

<<chipPeace characterSprite>>
chip: *sigh* the faster we finish cleaning, the sooner we can get down to business. where do you wanna start?

<<empty characterSprite>>
freddie: guys it's the physics part of the physics game whoaaaa (cheer)

===
title: RagdollTime
---
<<empty characterSprite>>
lucifer: okay, so we're gonna start here! in the living room. 

chip: mhm... this looks manageable.

lucifer: yeah! uh... cool, i'm exhausted so i'm just gonna hang out here, let me know if you don't know where to put something.

chip: oh, so what you meant by help is that I'M doing all the work?

lucifer: hahaha, kinda! i wanna watch you get all sweaty carrying my stuff around, is that so wrong?

===
title: AppleInteract
---
narrator: chip picks up the apple and rotates it around in his hand.
lucifer: ohh, that was gonna be my lunch today! loooove those things.
chip: this was... this isn't a meal, this is a snack at best.
lucifer: well, it's a meal when you can't afford anything else. ooh, wait, i have a question for you!
chip: ask away.
lucifer: favorite type of apple? there's a wrong answer, by the way. several wrong answers. sooo many wrong answers.
chip: can't say i have strong apple opinions, but i guess i fuck with honeycrisps. and whatever the yellow ones are called.
lucifer: honeycrisp is a good answer... ehehehehe
lucifer: oh, you can keep going. i'll stop distracting you!

===
title: BrickInteract
---
chip: a brick? why do you just have a brick?
lucifer: that thing was my doorstop for the loooongest time.
lucifer: like, i'd go outside to take the trash out and would leave the door propped open so i could, like, come back in. and not have to bring my keys.
chip: your door auto-locks?
lucifer: yeah, it's kind of annoying. do you know how many times i've been locked out?
narrator: chip chuckles.
chip: loads of times, i'm guessing. what made you retire the brick?
lucifer: someone came in while i was downstairs.
chip: oh.
lucifer: ... yeah.

===
title: ClarinetInteract
---
narrator: it's a clarinet! it looks well-taken care of, as far as chip's aware.
chip: does this thing have a case?
lucifer: oh! yeah, yeah, it's over in my room. if you want to leave that out, that's fine by me.
lucifer: i was just working on some stuff for class.
chip: ...class?
lucifer: grad school. uh, getting my master's in clarinet performance. 
chip: ohhh, that's cool. wouldn't have taken you for an orchestra guy. you seem more like a my chemical romance type.
lucifer: haha, hey, i contain multitudes. who's to say i can't be both?
chip: fair enough. yeah, i played cello back in high school. a lifetime ago.
lucifer: oh, please, "a lifetime"? you don't look THAT old.
chip: thank– pause. i don't look "THAT" old? what's that supposed to mean?
narrator: lucifer shrugs, attempting to suppress a smile.

===
title: EnvelopeInteract
---
narrator: chip picks up an envelope addressed to one "lucifer devoy". from the general hospital a little ways away.
narrator: it's been opened and haphazardly resealed. he holds it up, in between two fingers.
chip: yo, luce, where do you want me to put this?
lucifer: ohhhhh that... uh, just leave it on the desk. i've still gotta pay that.
chip: ah, right.
lucifer: yeah, they've been up my ass for a couple of weeks, but i dunno what they want me to do, like...
lucifer: i can't pull a couple thousand dollars out of thin air, y'know?
chip: yikes. no, that's insane. uh, i'll leave it there, then.
lucifer: aw, you're not even gonna offer to pay it off for me?
lucifer: it's like you don't even care...
chip: i'm not your sugar daddy, dude, my bank account is in the negatives.
lucifer: wowww we're twinningggg!

